Z||000000||Punkndrublic||03-03-99||08:34 PM||||I have two 12" Phoenix Gold Saphires. I did some preliminary measurements and it looks as if they ll just barely fit in the front ( i have no A/C ) Has anybody tried this?? the subs only need 2 cubic feet each.
Z||000001||John Johnston||03-04-99||12:07 AM||||Check out the discussion in the general topics part of this forum.
Z||000002||DaRkLoRD||03-04-99||12:18 AM||||2 12"s in the front of a Fiero. Interesting. ;)<br>the best site I've seen so far for that topic is this one:<br>http://www.perigee.net/~lunapark/<p>they installed 2 10" subs in the front. 
Z||000003||cmore||03-11-99||07:38 PM||||Simple answer here "don't put subs in the front of back of a Fiero" ! I've spent the past 5 years experimenting on where to put subs. I tried a 10 up front which was alright but 90% of the sound went outside the car. I also tried dual 10's in the trunk with a long port but there was no bass at all. So I ended up cutting the carpet and insulation off the firewall behind the seat. I put a 10" JL behind the passenger seat and 3 amps behind the drivers seat. I also have 4x10 alpines in the dash with alpine bass engines under the seat. Check out my Fiero page for more information on my stereo.<p>http://frontpage.erie.net/cmore/fieropag.htm
Z||000004||spike||03-23-99||04:25 PM||||I built a box that covered the whole back window of the fiero. the subs fired at the back of my head. I put 2 10 inch subs, amp was installed in middle glove compartment after i removed the door. I also made a plexglass window in the box so i could see behind me. i finished it with matching gray vynle. the box fit in very tight. i did not have to screw it in place. it looked custom. the box costed about 50.00 canadian. I am going to build another one for my next fiero.
Z||000005||BlkFiero||04-09-99||11:42 AM||||I have a custom box i built using fiberglass it fit on the passengers side where it dips in for your feet it was the right size for a 10. the box looks great. It dosent take that much leg room away form the passenger and it relly pounds. I have a pioneer 10 and a mtx 240 amp, alpine 4x10 , and a kenwood cd. I dont think that there is enough room up front for two 12s 
